<ul>
<li>
<p>Wifi connectivity.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Bluetooth connectivity.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The ability to change colors.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A touch screen.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A control panel of any kind.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A subscription service, giving users access to bug-related podcasts and a biweekly Substack wherein experts from across the pest-control industry share tips and stories from their careers.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>A sensor that tells what kinds of bugs you’ve trapped.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>An app that creates graphs, tracks peak time of insect activity, and awards cheekily-named badges (such as ‘the gnatural’ and ‘pretty fly’) based on insect variety and traffic.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>An internal artificial intelligence that analyzes data to provide suggestions for where to install additional traps and offer purchase suggestions based on your bug-trapping history.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Stickers to be placed in each window, informing neighborhood bugs that your house is protected by Raid Essentials Flying Insect Light Traps.</p>
</li>
</ul>